'''''Reign of the Empire: Edge of the Abyss''''' is a [[canon]] novel and the second volume of the ''[[Star Wars: Reign of the Empire]]'' trilogy. It was written by [[Rebecca Roanhorse]] and published by [[Random House Worlds]] on [[September 15]], [[2026]]. An [[Reign of the Empire: Edge of the Abyss (audiobook)|audiobook version]] was released along side the novel. It is set in [[6 BBY]], one [[Standard year|year]] before the [[Andor Season 1|first season]] of the television series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]''.

==Publisher's summary==
'''''In this thrilling sequel to'' The Mask of Fear,'' set one year before season one of ''Andor'', truth becomes a weapon of the Empire.'''''

''Over a decade into the Empire's reign, life under Imperial rule has become routine. The days of the Republic have long passed into memory—if they are remembered at all.''

''Within the Senate, Mon Mothma and Bail Organa face dwindling influence, for there is no difference between the will of the Emperor and the direction of his Empire. Bail increasingly shifts his focus to support clandestine resistance efforts, knowing a successful fight against the Empire will come from beyond the halls of power. Meanwhile, Mon Mothma sees one chance to take a stand when she makes a horrifying discovery about the lengths the regime will go to weaponize truth and loyalty. The Empire's newest target: the next generation raised under the Emperor's ever deepening shadow, including Mon and Bail's daughters.''

''Across the galaxy, disparate rebel factions are rendered outcasts, branded criminals, and pitted against each other. On Ghorman, an idealistic student group seeks to make meaningful change, unaware of the ISB agent who seeks to sabotage them from the inside. Leaders like Saw Gerrera and Anto Kreegyr squabble and bargain to survive one more day against the crush of Imperial might. Trust is rare and betrayal quick. A distracted, disorganized resistance is one that is easy to snuff out. There are few heroes…and no alliances.''

''When one of Gerrera's partisans is captured by the Empire, time is running out for senators, outcasts, spies, and all those that desire a better tomorrow. What the prisoner knows could help the Empire eradicate any whisper of resistance, end any rebellion before it can truly begin—and ensure that the Empire's truth is all the galaxy will ever know.''

==Development==
{{Quote|I believe we are in crisis. The distance between what is said and what is known to be true has become an abyss. Of all the things at risk, the loss of an objective reality is perhaps the most dangerous. The death of truth is the ultimate victory of evil.|Mon Mothma in ''Star Wars: Andor''|<ref name="Welcome">{{Andor|Welcome to the Rebellion}}</ref>}}
[[File:MonMothmaKnowntobeTrue-WelcometotheRebellion.png|thumb|left|300px|In ''Star Wars: Andor'', Mon Mothma declared that "The distance between what is said and what is known to be true has become an abyss" in her final speech to the Imperial Senate, a line which inspired the title of ''Edge of the Abyss''.]]
The novel was first announced on [[July 29]], [[2024]]. Initially simply known as "book two" of the ''[[Star Wars: Reign of the Empire]]'' trilogy, the novel was announced to be written by [[Rebecca Roanhorse]] and planned to be published by [[Random House Worlds]] in spring [[2026]].<ref name="Gizmodo" /> On [[February 3]], [[2025]], [[Alexander Freed]], author of [[Reign of the Empire: The Mask of Fear|the first novel]], reported that Roanhorse was "already hard at work" on her novel.<ref name="Freed 3 Weeks">{{Bluesky|alexandermfreed.bsky.social|post/3lhcy6zqpjk2v|[[Alexander Freed]]|date=2025-02-03|quote=So The Mask of Fear is out in three weeks. Rebecca Roanhorse is already hard at work on the actual follow up (and it will, from what I've seen, be grand!) But I'm vaguely curious about what happens if you read all the Alexander Freed Star Wars novels in chronological order. Do they work as a whole?}}</ref> Tom Hoeler also said that ideas introduced in the 2024 in-universe history book ''[[Star Wars: The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]'' by [[Chris Kempshall]] would also be explored in the novel.<ref name="Rise Inspired">{{Twitter|DarthInternous|status/1817952147222282346|[[Tom Hoeler]]|date=2024-07-29|quote=I may or may not have sent Rebecca some notes based on tidbits in your book that said "ooo let's explore this"}} {{C|In response to: "I'm choosing to believe that there was just a photo of me on all of your desks for this and the 'do it for him' Simpsons message."}}</ref>

During the [[Wikipedia:San Diego Comic-Con|San Diego Comic-Con]] on [[July 25]], 2025, the novel's title was revealed to be ''Reign of the Empire: Edge of the Abyss'' and the release date got pushed to fall 2026. The book's title is taken from part of [[Mon Mothma]]'s speech from the ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'' [[Andor Season 2|Season 2]] episode<ref name="IG">{{Instagram|url=p/DMlJiHDs5RJ|username=rebeccaroanhorse|name=[[Rebecca Roanhorse]]|quote=Title and updated release date of my upcoming STAR WARS novel announced at SDCC. THE EDGE OF THE ABYSS takes place a year before Andor S1. “ I believe we are in crisis. The distance between what is said and what is known to be true has become an abyss. Of all the things at risk, the loss of an objective reality is perhaps the most dangerous. The death of truth is the ultimate victory of evil.” - Mon Mothma, Andor ep S2E9}}</ref> "[[Welcome to the Rebellion]]" of her [[Escape from the Senate|denouncing]] the [[Ghorman Massacre]] in the [[Imperial Senate]].<ref name="Welcome" /> The book's cover was revealed on [[March 10]], [[2026]], along with the announcement that a number of characters from ''Andor'' would be appearing.<ref name="Cover">{{WebCite|url=https://gizmodo.com/star-wars-reign-of-the-empire-2-edge-of-abyss-cover-reveal-andor-2000731925|text=The Next 'Star Wars' Book Sets the Stage for the 'Andor' Revolution (Exclusive)|author=James Whitbrook|date=2026-03-10|work=[[Wikipedia:Gizmodo|''Gizmodo'']]|archivedate=20260310164633}}</ref>
More details were later revealed during the San Diego Comic-Con in July 2026.<ref name="SDCC2026">{{WebCite|archivedate=20260725030851|text=SDCC ’26 Publishing Panels Roundup: Luke & Leia Jedi Training Novel, Mad Cave’s X-Wing Academy, and More!|url=https://mynockmanor.com/sdcc-26-publishing-panels-roundup-luke-leia-jedi-training-novel-mad-caves-x-wing-academy-and-more/|author=Head Butler Ryan}}</ref>

